# Global Hub UI changes (no forks)

When changing **main styling, layout, UX patterns, boxes, headers, tables, tabs, forms, or hover/interaction chrome**, update the **shared tokens / shared components** and wire every surface through them. Do not fix one page and leave forks elsewhere.

## Do this

1. Change the **source of truth** first: `src/lib/hub/shellTokens.ts`, `src/app/globals.css` Hub classes, `HubMetadataStatGrid`, `GameOverviewTitleBlock`, `DAppSectionHeader` / `GameSectionHeader`, `KxDataTable`, `CovenantDatetimeField`, shared form field chrome, etc.
2. Replace local one-offs (`rounded-* border bg-*`, hardcoded `#02abb8`, custom title stacks) with those shared pieces.
3. Sweep **all** Hub products that use the same pattern: Tokens, dApps, Store, Games, Chronicles, Magazines, vBlog, Ads, Rewards / covenant widgets.
4. Prefer content-smart layouts (short metadata → 2-up; long ids/txs → full width) from one helper, not per-page grids.
5. Push the shared change so production stays one look.

## Do not

- Patch only Tokens (or only Store / only one dApp) when the pattern is Hub-wide.
- Invent a second metadata box, section header, datetime preset row, or table chrome for a single screen.
- Leave `compact` / “temporary” visual forks that change title size, tilt, or dividers.

